    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0471" n="1305" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/195a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-28T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 28, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>697. Referring your 1850, January 23, 2 p.m., following delivered today by War
                    Trade Board to Danish Minister, Washington: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>It seems wise, in order to avoid the possibility of future
                            misunderstanding, to say to Your Excellency that, in case our countries
                            are fortunate enough to reach an agreement, the conditions in our letter
                            of January 16 [<hi rendition="#italic">17</hi>], respecting Denmark’s
                            export to the Central Powers of butter, bacon, fish, cattle, and horses
                            will be held by us to apply as of and from the date of our said
                            letter.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
